{
  "title": "Salat of وَ وَاعَدْنَا",
  "data": "Wa Wa'adna Prayer\nOn each of the first ten nights of Dhul Hijjah, between the Maghrib and Isha prayers, offer a prayer of two units.\nIn each unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once, [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) once, and this verse of [Surah al-A'raf](A11) (7:142):\nوَوٰعَدْنَا مُوْسٰى ثَلٰثِيْنَ لَيْلَةً وَّاَتْمَمْنٰهَا بِعَشْرٍ فَتَمَّ مِيْقَاتُ رَبِّهٖۤ اَرْبَعِيْنَ لَيْلَةً  ۚ\nWA WAA'ADNAA MOOSAA THALAATHEENA LAYLATAN WA ATMAMNAAHAA BI-A'SHRIN FATAMMA MEEQAATU RABBIHEE ARBA'EENA LAYLAH\nAnd We appointed with Moses a time of thirty nights and completed them with ten more, so the appointed time of his Lord was complete forty nights,\nوَقَالَ مُوْسٰى لِاَخِيْهِ هٰرُوْنَ اخْلُفْنِىْ فِىْ قَوْمِىْ وَاَصْلِحْ وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ سَبِيْلَ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(142)\nWA QAALA MOOSAA LI-AKHEEHI HAAROONAKH LUFNEE FEE QAWMEE WA ASLIH WA LAA TATTABI' SABEELAL MUFSIDEEN\nand Moses said to his brother Aaron: Take my place among my people, and act well and do not follow the way of the mischief-makers.\nIt is also recommended to fast the first nine days of Dhul Hijjah.",
  "tabs": [
    "Dua after Fajr & Maghrib\nFrom the first of Dhul Hijjah until the eve of Arafah, recite after the Fajr and Maghrib prayers:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ هٰذِهِ الْاَيَّامُ الَّتِيْ فَضَّلْتَهَا عَلَى الْاَيَّامِ وَشَرَّفْتَهَا\nALLAAHUMMA HAADHIHIL AYYAAMUL LATEE FADDALTAHAA A'LAL AYYAAMI WA SHARRAFTAHAA\nO Allah, these days that You have preferred and favored on other days,\nقَدْ بَلَّغْتَنِيْهَا بِمَنِّكَ وَرَحْمَتِكَ\nQAD BALLAGHTANEEHAA BIMANNIKA WA RAHMATIK\nYou have allowed me to attain them out of Your favor and mercy;\nفَاَنْزِلْ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ بَرَكَاتِكَ وَاَوْسِعْ عَلَيْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ نَعْمَاۤئِكَ\nFA-ANZIL A'LAYNAA MIN BARAKAATIKA WA AWSI' A'LAYNAA FEEHAA MIN NA'MAA'IK\nso, (please) descend on us Your blessings and expand for us Your boons.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْۤ اَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, I beseech you to send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad\nوَاَنْ تَهْدِيَنَا فِيْهَا لِسَبِيْلِ الْهُدٰى وَالْعَفَافِ وَالْغِنٰى وَالْعَمَلِ فِيْهَا بِمَا تُحِبُّ وَتَرْضٰىۤ\nWA AN TAHDIYANAA FEEHAA LISABEELIL HUDAA WAL A'FAAFI WAL GHINAA WAL A'MALI FEEHAA BIMAA TUHIBBU WA TARDAA\nand to guide us on these days to the path of guidance, chastity, sufficiency, and doing that which You like and please.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْۤ اَسْاَلُكَ يَا مَوْضِعَ كُلِّ شَكْوٰى وَيَا سَامِعَ كُلِّ نَجْوٰى\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA YAA MAWDI'A KULLI SHAKWAA WA YAA SAAMI'A KULLI NAJWAA\nO Allah, I beseech You, O object of all complaints, O Hearer of all confidential talks,\nوَيَا شَاهِدَ كُلِّ مَلَاٍ وَيَا عَالِمَ كُلِّ خَفِيَّةٍ\nWA YAA SHAAHIDA KULLI MALA'IN WA YAA A'ALIMA KULLI KHAFIYYAH\nO Attendant in all sessions, O Knower of all hidden matters,\nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nto send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَاَنْ تَكْشِفَ عَنَّا فِيْهَا الْبَلَاۤءَ وَتَسْتَجِيْبَ لَنَا فِيْهَا الدُّعَاۤءَ\nWA AN TAKSHIFA A'NNAA FEEHAL BALAA'A WA TASTAJEEBA LANAA FEEHAD DU'AA'\nrelieve us from all hardships on these days, respond to our prayers,\nوَتُقَوِّيَنَا فِيْهَا وَتُعِيْنَنَا وَتُوَفِّقَنَا فِيْهَا لِمَا تُحِبُّ رَبَّنَا وَتَرْضٰى\nWA TUQAWWIYANAA FEEHAA WA TU'EENANAA WA TUWAFFIQANAA FEEHAA LIMAA TUHIBBU RABBANAA WA TARDAA\ngrant us power, aid us, and lead us successfully to all that which You, O our Lord, like and please\nوَعَلٰى مَا افْتَرَضْتَ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ طَاعَتِكَ وَطَاعَةِ رَسُوْلِكَ وَاَهْلِ وِلَايَتِكَ\nWA A'LAA MAF TARADTA A'LAYNAA MIN TAA'ATIKA WA TAA'ATI RASOOLIKA WA AHLI WILAAYATIK\nand to do acts of obedience to You that which You have made obligatory upon us as well as acts of obedience to Your Messenger and to the men of Your leadership.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْۤ اَسْاَلُكَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEENA AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, I beseech You, O most Merciful of all those who show mercy, to send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad\nوَاَنْ تَهَبَ لَنَا فِيْهَا الرِّضَا اِنَّكَ سَمِيْعُ الدُّعَاۤءِ\nWA AN TAHABA LANAA FEEHAR RIDAA INNAKA SAMEE'UD DU'AA'\nand grant us [Your] pleasure on these days. You are verily Hearer of prayers.\nوَلَا تَحْرِمْنَا خَيْرَ مَا تُنْزِلُ فِيْهَا مِنَ السَّمَاۤءِ\nWA LAA TAHRIMNAA KHAYRA MAA TUNZILU FEEHAA MINAS SAMAA'\nDo not deprive us of the good that You cause to come down from the heavens on these days,\nوَطَهِّرْنَا مِنَ الذُّنُوْبِ يَا عَلَّامَ الْغُيُوْبِ\nWA TAHHIRNAA MINADH DHUNOOBI YAA A'LLAAMAL GHUYOOB\npurify us from sins, O Knower of all unseen things,\nوَاَوْجِبْ لَنَا فِيْهَا دَارَ الْخُلُوْدِ\nWA AWJIB LANAA FEEHAA DAARAL KHULOOD\nand make certain for us the abode of immortality.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad\nوَلَا تَتْرُكْ لَنَا فِيْهَا ذَنْبًا اِلَّا غَفَرْتَهٗ وَلَا هَمًّا اِلَّا فَرَّجْتَهٗ\nWA LAA TATRUK LANAA FEEHAA DHANBAN ILLAA GHAFARTAHOO WA LAA HAMMAN ILLAA FARRAJTAH\nand do not leave for us a sin but that You forgive it, no depression but that You relieve it,\nوَلَا دَيْنًا اِلَّا قَضَيْتَهٗ وَلَا غَاۤئِبًا اِلَّاۤ اَدَّيْتَهٗ\nWA LAA DAYNAN ILLAA QADAYTAHOO WA LAA GHAA'IBAN ILLAA ADDAYTAH\nno debt but that You help us settle it, no absent but that You make join us,\nوَلَا حَاجَةً مِنْ حَوَاۤئِجِ الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ اِلَّا سَهَّلْتَهَا وَيَسَّرْتَهَا\nWA LAA HAAJATAN MIN HAWAA'IJID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRATI ILLAA SAHHALTAHAA WA YASSARTAHAA\nand no need in this world and the Next World but that You make it easy and obtainable.\nاِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْ‏ءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nINNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nYou, verily, have power over all things.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ يَا عَالِمَ الْخَفِيَّاتِ يَا رَاحِمَ الْعَبَرَاتِ يَا مُجِيْبَ الدَّعَوَاتِ\nALLAAHUMMA YAA A'ALIMAL KHAFIYYAATI YAA RAAHIMAL A'BARAATI YAA MUJEEBAD DA'AWAAT\nO Allah! O Knower of all hidden things! O Merciful of all tears! O Answerer of all prayers!\nيَا رَبَّ الْاَرَضِيْنَ وَالسَّمَاوَاتِ يَا مَنْ لَا تَتَشَابَهُ عَلَيْهِ الْاَصْوَاتُ\nYAA RABBAL ARADEENA WAS SAMAAWAATI YAA MAN LAA TATASHAABAHU A'LAYHIL ASWAAT\nO Lord of the [layers of the] earth and the heavens! O He Who is not confused by various sounds!\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\n(Please) send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad\nوَاجْعَلْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ عُتَقَاۤئِكَ وَطُلَقَاۤئِكَ مِنَ النَّارِ\nWAJ'ALNAA FEEHAA MIN U'TAQAA'IKA WA TULAQAA'IKA MINAN NAAR\nand include us, on these days, with those whom You release and discharge from Hellfire,\nوَالْفَاۤئِزِيْنَ بِجَنَّتِكَ وَالنَّاجِيْنَ بِرَحْمَتِكَ\nWAL FAA'IZEENA BIJANNATIKA WAN NAAJEENA BIRAHMATIK\nthose whom You make win Your Paradise, and those whom You save, out of Your mercy.\nيَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO most Merciful of all those who show mercy!\nوَصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى سَيِّدِنَا مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nWA SALLALLAAHU A'LAA SAYYIDINAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE AJMA'EEN\nAllah may send blessings to our master, Muhammad, and to his entire Household.",
    "Five Testimonies\nOn each of the first ten days of Dhul Hijjah, recite these five testimonies, each 100 times (or at least 10 times):\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nASH-HADU AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nI bear witness that there is no god save Allah, alone without having any partner.\nلَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَلَهُ الْحَمْدُ بِيَدِهِ الْخَيْرُ\nLAHUL MULKU WA LAHUL HAMDU BIYADIHIL KHAYR\nHis is the kingdom and His is all praise. In His Hand is all goodness,\nوَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْ‏ءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nWA HUWA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nand He has power over all things.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nASH-HADU AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nI bear witness that there is no god save Allah, alone without having any partner.\nاَحَدًا صَمَدًا لَمْ يَتَّخِذْ صَاحِبَةً وَلَا وَلَدًا\nAHADAN SAMADAN LAM YATTAKHIDH SAAHIBATAN WA LAA WALADAA\nOne and Only and Besought of all. He has not taken to Himself wife nor son.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nASH-HADU AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nI bear witness that there is no god save Allah, alone without having any partner,\nاَحَدًا صَمَدًا لَمْ يَلِدْ وَلَمْ يُوْلَدْ وَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَهٗ كُفُوًا اَحَدٌ\nAHADAN SAMADAN LAM YALID WA LAM YOOLAD WA LAM YAKUN LAHOO KUFUWAN AHAD\nOne and Only and Besought of all. He begets not, nor is He begotten, and there is none comparable to Him.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nASH-HADU AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nI bear witness that there is no god save Allah, alone without having any partner.\nلَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَلَهُ الْحَمْدُ يُحْيِيْ وَيُمِيْتُ\nLAHUL MULKU WA LAHUL HAMDU YUHYEE WA YUMEET\nHis is the kingdom and His is all praise. He brings to life and causes to die,\nوَهُوَ حَيٌّ لَا يَمُوْتُ بِيَدِهِ الْخَيْرُ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْ‏ءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nWA HUWA HAYYUN LAA YAMOOTU BIYADIHIL KHAYRU WA HUWA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nand He is Ever-living and never dies. In His Hand is all goodness and He has power over all things.\nحَسْبِيَ اللّٰهُ وَكَفٰى سَمِعَ اللّٰهُ لِمَنْ دَعَا\nHASBIYALLAAHU WA KAFAA SAMI'ALLAAHU LIMAN DA'AA\nSufficient to me is Allah and nothing else. May Allah listen from him who prays to Him.\nلَيْسَ وَرَاۤءَ اللّٰهِ مُنْتَهٰى اَشْهَدُ لِلّٰهِ بِمَا دَعَا\nLAYSA WARAA'ALLAAHI MUNTAHAA ASH-HADU LILLAAHI BIMAA DA'AA\nThere is no end beyond Allah. I bear witness to Allah for all that He has declared,\nوَاَنَّهٗ بَرِيْۤ‏ءٌ مِمَّنْ تَبَرَّاَ وَاَنَّ لِلّٰهِ الْاٰخِرَةَ وَالْاُوْلٰى\nWA ANNAHOO BAREE'UN MIMMAN TABARRA'A WA ANNA LILLAAHIL AAKHIRATA WAL OOLAA\nHe is clear of all that from which He has declared clearness, and Allah’s is the end and the beginning of all things.",
    "Tahlil of Imam Ali\nOn each of the first ten days of Dhul Hijjah, recite, preferably 10 times a day:\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عَدَدَ اللَّيَالِيْ وَالدُّهُوْرِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU A'DADAL LAYAALEE WAD DUHOOR\nThere is no god save Allah as many as nights and ages.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عَدَدَ اَمْوَاجِ الْبُحُوْرِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU A'DADA AMWAAJIL BUHOOR\nThere is no god save Allah as many as the waves of oceans.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَرَحْمَتُهٗ خَيْرٌ مِمَّا يَجْمَعُوْنَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WA RAHMATUHOO KHAYRUN MIMMAA YAJMA'OON\nThere is no god save Allah and His mercy is better than what they amass.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عَدَدَ الشَّوْكِ وَالشَّجَرِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU A'DADASH SHAWKI WASH SHAJAR\nThere is no god save Allah as many as thorns and trees.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عَدَدَ الشَّعْرِ وَالْوَبَرِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU A'DADASH SHA'RI WAL WABAR\nThere is no god save Allah as many as hairs and piles.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عَدَدَ الْحَجَرِ وَالْمَدَرِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU A'DADAL HAJARI WAL MADAR\nThere is no god save Allah as many as stones and loams.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عَدَدَ لَمْحِ الْعُيُوْنِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU A'DADA LAMHIL U'YOON\nThere is no god save Allah as many as sights of eyes.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ فِي اللَّيْلِ اِذَا عَسْعَسَ وَالصُّبْحِ اِذَا تَنَفَّسَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU FIL LAYLI IDHAA A'S'ASA WAS SUBHI IDHAA TANAFFAS\nThere is no god save Allah in the night when it departs and in the morning when it brightens.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عَدَدَ الرِّيَاحِ فِي الْبَرَارِيْ وَالصُّخُوْرِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU A'DADAR RIYAAHI FIL BARAAREE WAS SUKHOOR\nThere is no god save Allah as much as wind in lands and rocks.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ مِنَ الْيَوْمِ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يُنْفَخُ فِي الصُّوْرِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU MINAL YAWMI ILAA YAWMI YUNFAKHU FIS SOOR\nThere is no god save Allah from this day up to the day when the Trumpet will be blown."
  ],
  "merits": "Wa Wa'adna Prayer: the reward of offering this prayer is to participate in the rewards of those who go on Hajj.\n\nFasting: to fast on the first nine days of Dhul Hijjah is equal to the fasting of one's whole lifetime.\n\nDua after Fajr & Maghrib: Shaykh al-Tusi and Sayyid Ibn Tawus report this supplicatory prayer from Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.).\n\nFive Testimonies: Archangel Gabriel has conveyed these five testaments as gift of Almighty Allah to Prophet Jesus (a.s.) and instructed him to say them on the first ten days of Dhul Hijjah. An excellent reward has been mentioned to be for whoever repeats these five statements one hundred times each day. However, 'Allamah al-Majlisi says that it is not improbable that each of these five testaments is repeated ten times each day. Yet, to repeat them one hundred times is better.\n\nTahlil of Imam Ali: this doxology is reported from Imam Ali Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.), and an excellent reward has been reported for those saying it on the first ten days of Dhul Hijjah."
}
